data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The `ROLLBACK` action logic is now confirmed. The savepoint's offset check (R23b) ensures all savepoints set at a *larger offset* are removed, while retaining the current savepoint `s`. This prevents inconsistencies by truncating the write list correctly. The implementation aligns with the specification and maintains the write list size constraints.\n\nThe `CHECKPOINT` action (R23c) requires no modifications to the transaction's state, according to the specifications. The `READ` action (R23d) now only requires adding the read `key` to the `readSet`.\n\nNow, reviewing the final `Result` construction (Section 7.4). The `state` uses a `LinkedHashMap` wrapped in `Collections.unmodifiableMap` to ensure a deterministic iteration order, reflecting only the effects of committed transactions. The `committed` and `aborted` lists are also wrapped in `Collections.unmodifiableList`, preserving the log order of events as specified. The `incomplete` state uses a `TreeMap` to ensure deterministic ordering of open transactions.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The final `Result` construction now correctly uses immutable collections.  The `state` map uses `Collections.unmodifiableMap(new LinkedHashMap<>())`. Both `committed` and `aborted` lists now use `Collections.unmodifiableList(new ArrayList<>())`. The incomplete transactions are represented by `Collections.unmodifiableList(new ArrayList<>(openTxns.keySet()))`. This is efficient and correct. The `Result` construction is now finalized.\n\nManually verifying example scenarios against the logic confirms correct behavior, addressing edge cases and ensuring data consistency. The test cases demonstrate correct results.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The edge cases, including header validation and frame structure checks, are verified. Specific examples are constructed and tested. These validations are crucial for log integrity. The examples cover truncated logs, checksum mismatches, and various transaction scenarios, including begin/commit/rollback/savepoint combinations. The tests cover a diverse set of examples, validating all logic.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

