data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"`N < 6`: `MALFORMED_PAYLOAD` exception, as expected. If `k == 0`: `N >= 6`, but since no value follows, rule R13 (READ) triggers `MALFORMED_PAYLOAD` before R15 could apply `BAD_KEY` (key validation). The order of R13 and R15 is crucial for this validation. PUT/DELETE follows the same logic, R13 before R15.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The payload validation now considers all bounds. Examining the `READ` record's format, the analysis confirms that every offset read, related to `k`, `f`, and `v`, remains strictly within the payload's `n` bytes. The algorithm ensures no out-of-bounds reads.\n\nNow focusing on `CHECKPOINT` within rules R13, R14, and R19c. Specifically considering the case where `c` doesn't match `openTxns.size()` *and* one checkpoint listed ID is `0`. P4 states the check is `MALFORMED_PAYLOAD` before `BAD_TXN`.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"R14, BAD_TXN_ID (R14) precedes CHECKPOINT_MISMATCH (R19c) because R14 is checked first, validating checkpoint transaction IDs before comparing them to open transactions in R19c. Transaction ID 0xFFFFFFFF (4294967295L) confirms that `Long` comparison works correctly with `TreeMap`. BEGIN errors (R14, R17, R18) validation confirms that a bad transaction ID (0) triggers R14 (BAD_TXN_ID) before R17 (DUPLICATE_TXN) and R18 (TOO_MANY_OPEN). Savepoint/Rollback error precedence (R13, R14, R16a, R19, R19b) validation verifies R13 (MALFORMED_PAYLOAD) and R14 (BAD_TXN_ID) are properly enforced for invalid formats.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"R16a (BAD_NAME) precedes R19 (TXN_NOT_OPEN) for SAVEPOINT/ROLLBACK if the name is invalid and transaction is not open. R19 (TXN_NOT_OPEN) precedes R19b (NO_SAVEPOINT) if the transaction isn't open and savepoint doesn't exist, as per P4. READ record error precedence: MALFORMED_PAYLOAD -> BAD_TXN_ID -> BAD_KEY -> BAD_VALUE (if f==1) -> TXN_NOT_OPEN -> READ_MISMATCH. BAD_VALUE precedes TXN_NOT_OPEN when f==1 and the value is invalid within an open transaction. READ's key is added to readSet if TXN_NOT_OPEN is passed.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

