data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now reviewing the BEGIN record (Type 1) rules. R17 and R18 apply correctly: `DUPLICATE_TXN` triggered if the transaction ID is already present; `TOO_MANY_OPEN` if the maximum open transactions is exceeded. R20's implementation is accurate, correctly adding the transaction ID and its associated data to the appropriate data structures.\n\nPUT records (Type 2) are now under examination. R13 specifies payload length checks: `n` must meet specific criteria based on key and value lengths (`k` and `v`). R14 confirms a non-zero transaction ID. R15's key validation uses `checkKey()` to enforce length and byte range constraints.\n\nThe `checkKey` function is under review. The key's length must be within bounds (1-32 bytes). The individual key bytes must fall within the printable ASCII range. These checks are now confirmed. All checks work as defined.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

