data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now focusing on DELETE records (Type 3). Payload length, transaction ID, and key validations (R13, R14, R15) are being carefully checked to ensure format, non-zero ID, key length, and byte range requirements are enforced. The offset calculations and validation logic in `DELETE` are verified to maintain integrity. The structure for DELETE operations is implemented as specified by R15, following the same structure and payload offset validation as other record types.\n\nType 4 (COMMIT), now in focus, contains transaction ID validation (R14, requiring it to be non-zero). R19 confirms that the transaction must be open to proceed. Now, reviewing R22. R23 now concerns itself with ABORT, with R14 validating that transactions are not zero.\n\nType 5 (ABORT) verification now follows. Both R14 and R19 validation are implemented to check for a non-zero transaction ID (R14) and to confirm that the transaction exists in the list of open transactions (R19), confirming rule order. The processing ensures the integrity of the abort record.\n\nType 6 (SAVEPOINT) is being examined, which now applies R13 and R14. R13 specifies the payload size. R14 confirms the transaction ID is non-zero. R16a validates the name for printable ASCII characters. R19 ensures the transaction is open. The savepoint's validity is ensured.\n\nFocusing on Type 7 (ROLLBACK), now validating R13 to R19b. R13 checks the payload size against expected values. R14 requires the transaction ID to be non-zero. R16a checks the savepoint name for printable ASCII characters. R19 ensures the transaction exists in the list of open transactions. The existence of the savepoint in R19b is verified.\n\nNow examining Type 8 (CHECKPOINT). R13 validates the payload length. R14 requires a non-zero transaction ID for records within the list. The validation logic now checks payload size against expected values. The checkpoint ID check is verified to ensure each ID in the list.\n\nType 9 READ, being examined for R13 to R15 and R23d. Key and value rules now being confirmed. Correct payload handling and transaction validation, as well as a non-zero transaction ID. A key validation ensures compliance. Read set's integrity and consistency is confirmed.\n\nThe remaining cases are verified with a full trace, focusing on all the different scenarios to confirm the correct handling. The recovery logic is complete.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now verifying the commit record (Type 4).  R13 enforces payload length checks; R14 ensures a non-zero transaction ID. R19 confirms the transaction's presence in the open transactions list. R22 performs the conflict check and either applies the writes, aborts, and appends the transaction to `committed` or `aborted` lists. The transaction is removed from the `openTxns` map.\n\nExamining the abort record (Type 5). R13 mandates the payload length. R14 confirms a non-zero transaction ID. R19 verifies the transaction's existence in open transactions. R23 adds the aborted transaction to the `aborted` list and removes it from `openTxns`.\n\nThe savepoint record (Type 6) is validated. R13 checks the payload's size, and R14 ensures a non-zero transaction ID. R16a validates the savepoint name, and R19 confirms that the transaction is open.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

