data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"R13 and R14 are confirmed for CHECKPOINT records, checking payload size and transaction IDs. R19c validates the checkpoint list against open transactions, triggering CHECKPOINT_MISMATCH if sizes don't match, or if any transaction IDs are inconsistent, which confirms all transaction IDs in checkpoint records. R23c (checkpoint) now confirms the no-op, which completes its implementation.\n\nREAD record's initial R13 check verifies payload length against k (key length) and f (flags). MALFORMED_PAYLOAD is thrown if size mismatches.  R15 is under review. If flag f is set to 0, validating that length matches `6 + k`. If f is set to 1, length checks must include the additional value length `v`, making sure that length is at least `8 + k` and that length equals to `8 + k + v`. A `MALFORMED_PAYLOAD` exception is raised on mismatches.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

