data: {"id":"chatcmpl-9fb03431-7c52-4cc2-87d4-1d9b21530100","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544584,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The READ record processing now involves detailed byte-level verification to match the specification (Section 5.3). The layout is: `k` at payload byte 4, the key from bytes 5 to 4+`k`, `f` at 5+`k`, the value length `v` is a u16 at 6+`k` if f==1, and the value is from 8+`k` to 7+`k`+`v`. The corresponding exceptions are checked according to rules: `MALFORMED_PAYLOAD` triggers on size mismatches and `BAD_KEY` with bounds for the length and value. The rule's validity is confirmed with bytes `pay+8+k`, ensuring the algorithm follows the spec.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

